   "answer": "Task-CoEvolve uses the anchored difference estimator defined as \\(\\hat{S}(h) = \\frac{1}{N} \\sum_{t \\in T} \\bar{p}_t + \\frac{1}{N} \\sum_{t \\in S_k} \\frac{x_t(h) - \\bar{p}_t}{\\pi_t}\\) [3:15]. The raw outcome is not weighted directly because weighting the outcome \\(x_t(h)\\) by its inclusion probability \\(\\pi_t\\) would cause instability when tasks have small \\(\\pi_t\\) and historical success rates near 0 or 1, making the term \\(x_t(h)/\\pi_t\\) dominate and distort estimates [3:15]. Instead, anchoring the deviation \\(x_t(h) - \\bar{p}_t\\) ensures the estimator remains stable and comparable across iterations [3:15]."
  },
